{"name":"Shrimp Boudin","hex":"#dbbfa3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shrimp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of many swimming, often edible, crustaceans, chiefly of the infraorder Caridea or the suborder Dendrobranchiata, with slender legs, long whiskers and a long abdomen.","The flesh of such crustaceans."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish for shrimp.","To contract; to shrink."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shrimp"},{"term":"boudin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of blood sausage in French, Belgian, Luxembourgish and related cuisines.","A sausage in southern Louisiana Creole and Cajun cuisine, made from rice, ground pork (occasionally crawfish), and spices in a sausage casing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boudin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shrimp","blocks":[{"text":"A shrimp is a common name typically used for crustaceans with an elongated body and a primarily swimming mode of locomotion. The name usually refers to decapods belonging to the Caridea or Dendrobranchiata, although some crustaceans outside this order are also referred to as \"shrimp\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Palaemon_serratus_Croazia.jpg/330px-Palaemon_serratus_Croazia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrimp","wikidata":"Q1517781"},{"title":"Boudin","blocks":[{"text":"Boudin is a category of sausage - typically blood sausage - found in several French-speaking cultures. The added ingredients vary in French, Luxembourgish, Belgian, Swiss, Québecois, Acadian, Aostan, Louisiana Creole, and Cajun cuisine. Some variations such as boudin blanc contain no blood but retain the name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Boudin3.jpg/330px-Boudin3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boudin","wikidata":"Q13475519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Macrobrachium_carcinus.jpg/500px-Macrobrachium_carcinus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Macrobrachium_carcinus.jpg/1280px-Macrobrachium_carcinus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Macrobrachium_carcinus.jpg/500px-Macrobrachium_carcinus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bigclaw river shrimp from the Neotropics. Prawns are sometimes stated to be \"large shrimp\" or alternatively \"freshwater shrimp\", but this large-bodied, freshwater crustacean is a caridean shrimp, and is rarely referred to as a prawn.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMacrobrachium_carcinus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Lobster_NSRW_rotated2.jpg/500px-Lobster_NSRW_rotated2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Lobster_NSRW_rotated2.jpg/1280px-Lobster_NSRW_rotated2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Lobster_NSRW_rotated2.jpg/500px-Lobster_NSRW_rotated2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALobster_NSRW_rotated2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Panulirus_argus.png/120px-Panulirus_argus.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b5/Panulirus_argus.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or